{"step_index":196,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T21:20:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T05:20:44+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T05:20:44+08:00\nShowing lines 1-18 of 18\n1: # Changelog\n2: \n3: ## [1.0.0] - 2026-11-09\n4: ### Major\n5: - Initial release of Firebase Firestore-backed Quiz Web Application for Vercel deployment.\n6: - Added student quiz interface (`index.html`) faithfully retaining original visual styling with anti-cheat detection, countdown timer, auto-randomization, base64 result code, and JSON file export.\n7: - Added teacher authoring portal (`teacher.html`) with auto-numbered dynamic question cards, question/distractor editing inputs, options modal for quiz behavior toggles, and direct Firestore synchronization.\n8: - Added modular Firebase configuration and Firestore data access layer (`firebase-config.js`).\n9: - Added static routing configuration for Vercel deployment (`vercel.json`).\n10: \n11: ### Non-Major (Patch 1.0.1)\n12: - Replaced relative ES module imports in `index.html` and `teacher.html` with Firebase compat scripts loaded via Google's official CDN.\n13: - Why: Browsers block relative ES module file imports under the `file:///` protocol due to origin `null` CORS restrictions when opening HTML files directly from local storage. The compat scripts enable native dual-mode execution for both local double-clicking and cloud hosting on Vercel.\n14: \n15: ### Non-Major (Patch 1.0.2)\n16: - Updated quiz start rules in `index.html` to exact original phrasing with bold tags: `Each question has <b>20 seconds</b>. When time runs out, it moves on automatically with no points.` and `Every alt-tab or switch to another tab/app costs <b>-1 point</b>.`\n17: - Why: User requested direct copy of exact instruction text with bold emphasis on 20 seconds and violation deduction.\n18: "}
